# CODEOWNERS — SAFRS v1.1 R2/R3 review enforcement
#
# PLACEHOLDER OWNER — MUST BE REPLACED BY A HUMAN BEFORE THIS FILE PROVIDES ANY
# REAL CONTROL. `@sentra/safrs-maintainers` is a stand-in, not a verified GitHub
# team. Until a real team (or user) that actually exists in this organization is
# substituted, GitHub silently treats every rule below as having no valid owner
# and "Require review from Code Owners" will not block anything.
# Replacement is a governance action: it is itself an R2 change to this file.
#
# Derivation: every pattern in this file is derived from `.safrs/sensitive-paths.json`
# (`patterns`, `verification_control_patterns`, and `risk_overrides`). No pattern
# here is invented. Patterns are reproduced verbatim from that file, with a leading
# `/` added where the source pattern is root-anchored, so the mapping stays
# auditable line by line.
#
# Precedence warning: in CODEOWNERS the LAST matching pattern wins — it does not
# accumulate. Today every rule resolves to the same placeholder, so precedence is
# harmless. The moment a human assigns different owners per section, the ordering
# below becomes load-bearing: a broad rule placed after a narrow one will silently
# strip the narrow rule's owner. Re-verify ordering after any owner split.
#
# Related human-only setup that this file cannot perform on its own:
# see docs/governance/PLATFORM_ACTIVATION.md.

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# R2 — sensitive paths (source: sensitive-paths.json -> patterns, minimum_risk R2)
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

# Governance and security surfaces
/AGENTS.md                                      @sentra/safrs-maintainers
/SECURITY.md                                    @sentra/safrs-maintainers
/SAFRS_SPEC.md                                  @sentra/safrs-maintainers
/.safrs/**                                      @sentra/safrs-maintainers
/.github/workflows/**                           @sentra/safrs-maintainers
/.github/CODEOWNERS                             @sentra/safrs-maintainers

# Vendor instruction adapters
/CLAUDE.md                                      @sentra/safrs-maintainers
/GEMINI.md                                      @sentra/safrs-maintainers
/.agents/**                                     @sentra/safrs-maintainers
/.cursor/rules/**                               @sentra/safrs-maintainers

# Project capsule routing
/projects/**/AGENTS.md                          @sentra/safrs-maintainers

# Shared boundaries
/packages/**                                    @sentra/safrs-maintainers
/infrastructure/**                              @sentra/safrs-maintainers

# Root build and dependency manifests
/package.json                                   @sentra/safrs-maintainers
/pnpm-lock.yaml                                 @sentra/safrs-maintainers
/pnpm-workspace.yaml                            @sentra/safrs-maintainers
/turbo.json                                     @sentra/safrs-maintainers
/.github/renovate.json                          @sentra/safrs-maintainers

# Verification scripts and release evidence
/scripts/safrs-verify.mjs                       @sentra/safrs-maintainers
/scripts/safrs-verify.ps1                       @sentra/safrs-maintainers
/scripts/safrs-verify.sh                        @sentra/safrs-maintainers
/tests/repository/automation-policy.test.mjs    @sentra/safrs-maintainers
/docs/bootstrap/**                              @sentra/safrs-maintainers

# Security- and data-boundary directories at any depth
**/migrations/**                                @sentra/safrs-maintainers
**/auth/**                                      @sentra/safrs-maintainers
**/authorization/**                             @sentra/safrs-maintainers
**/security/**                                  @sentra/safrs-maintainers

# Dependency manifests at any depth
**/package.json                                 @sentra/safrs-maintainers
**/package-lock.json                            @sentra/safrs-maintainers
**/pnpm-lock.yaml                               @sentra/safrs-maintainers
**/yarn.lock                                    @sentra/safrs-maintainers
**/requirements*.txt                            @sentra/safrs-maintainers
**/pyproject.toml                               @sentra/safrs-maintainers
**/poetry.lock                                  @sentra/safrs-maintainers
**/Cargo.toml                                   @sentra/safrs-maintainers
**/Cargo.lock                                   @sentra/safrs-maintainers
**/go.mod                                       @sentra/safrs-maintainers
**/go.sum                                       @sentra/safrs-maintainers

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Verification-control surfaces
# (source: sensitive-paths.json -> verification_control_patterns)
# SAFRS-07: a change here receives equal or greater scrutiny than implementation.
# Entries already covered above are not repeated.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

/tools/safrs/**                                 @sentra/safrs-maintainers
**/tests/security/**                            @sentra/safrs-maintainers
**/tests/architecture/**                        @sentra/safrs-maintainers

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# R3 — high impact (source: sensitive-paths.json -> risk_overrides)
# These must NOT keep the same owner as the R2 block once real teams exist.
# R3 requires explicit human execution authorization on top of review; assign a
# narrower, higher-authority owner set here.
# Placed last deliberately so these rules win over any broader R2 rule above.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

/projects/**/safety-critical/**                 @sentra/safrs-maintainers
/projects/**/production/**                      @sentra/safrs-maintainers
/infrastructure/production/**                   @sentra/safrs-maintainers
